---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FurtherReading from '../../components/FurtherReading.astro';
import { ocean } from '../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import Interlude from '../../components/Interlude.astro';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'Transits', href: '/explore/transits/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Transits, the astrology of timing"
  description="Transits are the moving sky's aspects to your birth chart, astrology's timing technique. Learn how transits work, what retrogrades really mean, and how to use timing well."
  path="/explore/transits/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
      <h1>Transits: the astrology of timing</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Your birth chart is the fixed map; the sky keeps moving. Transits are what happens when
        today's planets form aspects to your natal ones: astrology's way of describing seasons,
        windows, and weather.
      </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img"
        src={ocean.currents.src}
        srcset={ocean.currents.srcset}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt={ocean.currents.alt}
        width={ocean.currents.width}
        height={ocean.currents.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>The weather metaphor, taken seriously</h2>
      <p>
        A transit doesn't make anything happen, any more than rain makes you cancel a picnic. It
        creates conditions in which some choices flow and others fight the current. Saturn
        crossing your Midheaven describes a season when career asks for structure and delivers
        earned results; what you build in it is entirely yours. Perspective, not prophecy.
      </p>
      <h2>Fast and slow weather</h2>
      <p>
        The Moon crosses your whole chart every month. Its transits are moods, gone by dinner.
        Mercury, Venus, and the Sun mark weeks; Mars, seasons. The slow outer planets, Jupiter
        through Pluto, define the chapters: Jupiter's roughly twelve-year cycle of growth,
        Saturn's twenty-nine-year curriculum (the famous Saturn returns near ages 29 and 58),
        and the once-per-lifetime visits of Uranus, Neptune, and Pluto to any given point.
        The slower the planet, the deeper the season.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Interlude
    image={ocean.dawnWave}
    eyebrow="Timing"
    heading="The slower the planet, the deeper the season."
    body="A transit creates conditions in which some choices flow and others fight the current. What you build in one is entirely yours."
  />


  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>About retrogrades</h2>
      <p>
        Retrograde motion is an optical effect, no planet ever backs up in space. Astrologically,
        a retrograde is a review season for that planet's themes: re-check, revise, reconsider,
        reconnect. Mercury retrograde, roughly three times a year, earns its reputation mostly by
        exposing what was rushed. It is a terrible scapegoat and a decent editor.
        <a href="/current-sky/">See what's retrograde right now.</a>
      </p>
      <h2>Using timing well</h2>
      <p>
        The practical questions a transit reading answers: What is this season for? What's coming
        in the next year, and when are the windows? Which decisions are better made now, and which
        gain from waiting? That's the territory of the timing readings:
        <a href="/readings/solar-return/">Solar Return</a> for the year,
        <a href="/readings/life-changes/">Life Changes</a> for a transition, and
        <a href="/readings/monthly-transits/">Monthly Personal Transits</a> for ongoing guidance.
      </p>
      <FurtherReading />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="What season are you in?"
    body="The Solar Return reading maps your personal year: what's active, what's emerging, and when to act."
    buttonLabel="About the Solar Return Reading"
    buttonHref="/readings/solar-return/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
